All done. Here's a summary of the implementation:

## Changes Made

### New Files
- **`core/auth/captcha.py`** — Captcha generation/verification module
  - 4-char codes from safe charset (no confusing chars)
  - Redis + in-memory dual storage with graceful degradation
  - L0 rate limiting: 3 fails → captcha invalidated + 60s IP cooldown

- **`tests/test_login_security.py`** — 15 test cases covering all security features

### Modified Files
- **`core/database/models.py`**
  - User: added `device_required`, `device_allowlist`, `locked_until` fields
  - New `LoginAudit` model for login audit logging

- **`core/auth/device_binding.py`**
  - Added `verify_user_device()` — account-level device binding (allowlist priority → global fallback)

- **`core/api/auth.py`**
  - `GET /auth/captcha` endpoint
  - Four-layer rate limiting (L1: IP+account 5/5min, L2: IP global 20/5min, L3: account 10/1h)
  - Anti-enumeration: user not found → 401 + virtual bcrypt timing
  - Register: now requires captcha (SMS code removed)
  - Send-code: captcha prerequisite added
  - Login audit logging on all auth events
  - Device binding integration via `verify_user_device`

- **`requirements.txt`** — Added `captcha>=0.5`, `Pillow>=10`

- **`tests/test_backend_integration.py`** — Updated existing tests for new captcha-based API

- **Frontend cleanup**: Removed all `8888`, `万能码`, `dev_code` references from `saas-register.html`, `welcome.html`, `login.html`

### Test Results
- **61 tests pass** (15 new + 46 existing, zero regressions)
- Frontend grep: 0 forbidden patterns found
